A shipment card: the order number and total, a status badge, the delivery progress, a timeline of steps and the
courier. A **block** composed from Badge, [Progress](<%= page_path(:progress) %>), Icon,
[Separator](<%= page_path(:separator) %>), Avatar and Button, as on the [Appica homepage](https://appica.dev/ui).

<%= embed Blocks::OrderTrackerPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
OrderTracker(number: order.number, items: order.items.count, total: order.total, currency: order.currency,
             status: order.shipment_status.to_sym, progress: order.shipment_progress) do
  OrderTimeline do
    order.tracking_events.each do |event|
      OrderStep(title: event.kind.to_sym, at: event.occurred_at, state: event.state.to_sym)
    end
  end
  OrderCourier(name: courier.first_name, avatar: courier.avatar_url, stops: courier.stops_left, href: tracking_url)
end
```

- `status:` picks the badge text and dot color: `:processing`, `:shipped`, `:in_transit`, `:out_for_delivery`,
  `:delivered`, `:delayed`.
- Steps are `:done` (a check), `:current` (a ringed dot, `aria-current="step"`) or `:upcoming` (a hollow dot, its
  time shown as an ETA). Times read relative to today: "Today, 11:05 AM", "Yesterday, 6:12 PM", "Jul 4, 9:41 AM".
- To update it live, re-render the card with a Turbo Stream `replace` when a tracking event arrives.

## Localization

`order_tracker.locales.yml` holds the statuses, the step titles given as symbols (`:confirmed`, `:shipped`,
`:sorting_hub`, `:local_facility`, `:out_for_delivery`, `:delivered`), the pluralized item and stop counts and the
date/time formats per language. Money uses the locale's currency format. Switch the **Locale** display option to try it.

